// WAKE, episode one: who was the man at the back of the wake? The
// investigation as cairn's design writes it, found out over lives: what the
// player carries is kept in `player`, what one life saw in `life`.
cast:
  margaret  "Margaret"   her eldest
facts (player):
  carried: set of his_name, her_hands
facts (life):
  met:   bool
  found: set of letter, photo
  said:  set of gave, hands
  hour:  int   (clock)
extern:
  name(who: ref of person) -> text

== the_stranger (quest)
  [title "Who was he?"] [scope player]
facts (player):
  stranger: ref of person   (role)
  asked: set of margaret, tom, danny

= noticed      when { met }
  [stage] [active spawn_stranger]
  A man nobody knows stood at the foot of the coffin. ^q1a9
= the_letter   when { found has letter }
  [objective] [after noticed] [active pin_letter]
  A letter signed "L.", from a city she never lived in. ^q1b2
= the_hands    when { said has hands }
  [objective] [optional] [after noticed]
  He said the hands were the same. ^q1c4
= late         when { since(noticed, hour) >= 3 }
  [stage] [after noticed]
  It is late, and he has not gone. ^q1c9
= named        when { the_letter and the_hands }
  [outcome] [after the_letter]
  [carried += his_name]
  He was {name(stranger)}, her son, from a life she didn't live. ^q1d7
= gone         when { hour >= 6 and not the_letter }
  [fails]
  He left before dawn. Nobody had his number. ^q1e3

== wake
At the back, a man nobody knows is crying harder than anyone. ^w1
[met = true]
* Ask Margaret who he is. ^w2
  MARGARET: I thought he was with you. ^w3
  [the_stranger.asked += margaret]
  -> drawer
* Look at his hands. ^w4
  [said += hands]
  [carried += her_hands]
  He has her hands. The same hands. ^w5
  -> drawer

== drawer
* Open the drawer. ^w6
  [found += letter]
  A letter, signed "L.". ^w7
  -> end
* Leave it. ^w8
  -> end
